From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MyNaai Dev <dev@mynaai.in>
Date: Wed, 5 Nov 2026 10:00:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Admin panel: Booking requests tab (leads, not bookings)

A new tab beside Bookings: the leads a customer sent, and what each salon did
with them.

Requests are NOT bookings. This tab reads `booking_requests` only — a booking
(the queue record) exists only after a salon accepts, and mixing the two is what
produces a conversion rate that adds up to more than 100%. An accepted request
shows here as Accepted and carries the `bookingId` it created: a pointer between
two separate records, never a merged row.

What it answers: are the salons getting leads, and are they answering them?

  · Tiles — Received / Accepted / Rejected / Auto-cancelled / Answer rate.
    Auto-cancelled is its OWN tile and is never folded into Rejected: a salon
    that misses leads has a staffing problem, a salon that turns them down has a
    pricing answer, and they are two different conversations. The buckets add up
    to Received.
  · Filters — salon (built from the report itself: the salons that actually got
    leads), status, date range (Today / 7 days / 30 days / All), and a search
    over customer name, customer phone and salon name.
  · The list — customer and phone, salon and city, requested day/time and
    services, estimated value, status, reply time, sent-at. Clicking a row opens
    the drawer.
  · The drawer — customer, requested services with prices (the snapshot taken at
    request time), and the LIFECYCLE: sent → accepted / rejected / auto-cancelled
    with timestamps and seconds. An auto-cancel reads "No answer within 60
    seconds — the slot was released automatically", never "rejected". If the
    request became a booking it links to it; otherwise the drawer says it never
    did.
  · The per-salon report — Received / Accepted / Rejected / Missed / Answer rate /
    Median reply, worst-first by Missed (the list an account manager works
    down). A salon that never answered shows a dash, not a zero: a zero reads as
    "instant reply". Sortable by missed / received / answer rate / slowest.
  · Export CSV — the FILTERED list, not the page on screen, with the API's own
    columns plus `response_seconds`. Built by walking the same endpoint, so a
    filter with 300 results exports 300 rows.

Rules honoured:

  · Read-only. An admin does not accept or reject on a salon's behalf; there is
    no "convert" button, because conversion happens when the salon accepts and a
    second path would produce two bookings.
  · A PENDING request past its window is DISPLAYED as auto-cancelled even if the
    sweeper has not written it yet — a page left open overnight never offers an
    "Awaiting answer" that nobody can answer.
  · Times are IST for every viewer, with one formatter.
  · The summary polls every 20 seconds (one query), so a lead that just arrived
    appears while somebody is watching.

Files

  new  src/pages/BookingRequests.jsx                  the tab
  new  src/components/BookingRequestDetailModal.jsx    the drawer + the status map
  mod  src/services/communication.jsx                  bookingRequestAPI
                                                       (adminList / adminSummary)
  mod  src/utils/TabArray.js                           the tab
  mod  src/App.jsx                                     /booking-requests route
                                                       behind ProtectedRoute

Backend it talks to: POST /api/bookingRequest/admin/list and /admin/summary
(patch `backend-2-booking-request-leads.patch`).

Verified: `vite build` passes with the page in the bundle.
